      "question": "Which ruff configuration is best for our service? Our workload and deployment constraints are not specified.",
      "before_sources": [],
      "after_sources": [
        {
          "path_or_url": "docs/configuration.md",
          "snippet": "Unlike [ESLint](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/use/configure/configuration-files#cascading-configuration-objects),\nRuff does not merge settings across configuration files; instead, the \"closest\" configuration file\nis used, and any parent configuration files are ignored. In lieu of this implicit cascade, Ruff\nsupports an [`extend`](settings.md#extend) field, which allows you to inherit the settings from another\nconfig file, like so:\n\n=== \"pyproject.toml\"",
          "line_start": 278,
          "line_end": 284
        },
        {
          "path_or_url": "docs/configuration.md",
          "snippet": "Ruff respects `pyproject.toml`, `ruff.toml`, and `.ruff.toml` files. All three implement an\nequivalent schema (though in the `ruff.toml` and `.ruff.toml` versions, the `[tool.ruff]` header and\n`tool.ruff` section prefix is omitted).\n\nFor a complete enumeration of the available configuration options, see [_Settings_](settings.md).",
          "line_start": 249,
          "line_end": 253
        }
      ]
    },
